    },
    {
      "title": "Compare stationary heights with the axis",
      "body": "<p>Use the sign of the leading coefficient and the heights of all extrema to decide when every monotonic branch crosses the axis.</p>",
      "recap": "Distinct polynomial roots are counted by combining end behaviour, monotonic pieces and stationary heights.",
      "pitfall": "A stationary point on the axis gives a repeated root, not two distinct crossings.",
      "pause": "Evaluate the heights, solve all required strict inequalities and intersect the parameter conditions.",
